{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_security_2026_09_19_full_application_audit_full_application_audit", "label": "Security Audit \u2014 Full Application (2026-09-19)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/security/2026-09-19-full-application-audit.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Scope stated with what it left out \u2014 deployed configuration, the skill's prompt-injection surface, denial of service by expensive queries \u2014 because an audit that does not say what it left out invites the reader to assume it covered everything."}, {"id": "docs_security_2026_09_19_full_application_audit_ssrf_dns_rebinding", "label": "Finding \u2014 Server-Side Request Forgery by DNS Rebinding (FIXED)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/security/2026-09-19-full-application-audit.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The checked address was discarded and the connection resolved the name a second time, so a short-TTL name answers public for the check and private for the connection. The recorded per-excerpt found/not-found result is an oracle against an internal endpoint, one guess at a time. Fixed by pinning Net::HTTP#ipaddr= to the address that passed the check, which leaves the Host header, SNI and certificate verification on the hostname."}, {"id": "docs_security_2026_09_19_full_application_audit_warnings_dismissed", "label": "Brakeman Warnings Dismissed (NOT EXPLOITABLE)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/security/2026-09-19-full-application-audit.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each read at the source rather than taken on its confidence rating: normalized input that cannot carry a quote, a Date from a closed case, a constant CRC lock key, literal table names, and a URL validated at append."}, {"id": "docs_security_2026_09_19_full_application_audit_what_held_up", "label": "What Held Up", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/security/2026-09-19-full-application-audit.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Established by reading so the next audit need not re-derive it: injection, dynamic dispatch guarded by a frozen KINDS list, no cookie surface on the API, PKCE-only OAuth, digest-only tokens, authorization, output escaping, mass assignment and redirects."}, {"id": "docs_security_2026_09_19_full_application_audit_smaller_notes", "label": "Smaller Notes (FIXED)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/security/2026-09-19-full-application-audit.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "None exploitable; each a habit worth not keeping \u2014 an interpolated quote rather than a bind, an interpolated table name, and a throttle that slept the whole minute regardless."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_security_2026_09_19_full_application_audit_full_application_audit", "target": "docs_security_2026_09_19_full_application_audit_ssrf_dns_rebinding", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/security/2026-09-19-full-application-audit.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_security_2026_09_19_full_application_audit_full_application_audit", "target": "docs_security_2026_09_19_full_application_audit_warnings_dismissed", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/security/2026-09-19-full-application-audit.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_security_2026_09_19_full_application_audit_full_application_audit", "target": "docs_security_2026_09_19_full_application_audit_what_held_up", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score"